WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Here's the check.

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:03.713
It reads each owner and each nominee once,

3
00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:06.695
with a single call and a
single read permission,

4
00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:11.513
so it can tell a member from a guest and
an enabled account from a disabled one.

5
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:13.274
Then it applies nine rules.

6
00:00:13.274 --> 00:00:17.877
The findings are the ones that block the
gate: no valid human owner, only one,

7
00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:22.706
a missing reference, a reference that
points at nothing or at a retired record,

8
00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:25.875
and a directory account
with no application owner.

9
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:29.063
Guests, bots and disabled
owners are warnings.

10
00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:33.380
And anything that might be a person
isn't checked until someone confirms it.
